# Mid Red report: Muse week 1 delivery manifest

Track: `asset_storytime_l2_unit1_pictures_20261025`. Phase 3, "Phase 3: Week 1 pictures".
Task: "Add failing tests for the Muse week 1 delivery manifest (Red)".

## The delivery contract that the tests encode

The specification amendment of 2026-11-01, decision 2, gives the contract. The PM words:

```text
PM decision (the shape of 11a06b9c stays the contract):
1. The Muse flow delivers the week 1 list rows.
2. At the delivery batch root, write one manifest.json in the 11a06b9c shape, with one entry per picture-list row.
3. job.id = the picture-list row id (for example l2-w01-story-page-hello-i-am-pat).
4. candidate.file = the approved 4000 x 3000 color print file, named as the list names it: <row id>-v1.png. lineArt.file = the approved 4000 x 3000 1-bit line-art print file: <row id>-line-v1.png. Copy the approved Muse print files to those names in the delivery folder; keep the Muse originals.
5. Workbooks matches the file name part only, so the folder prefix is free.
6. Only clean rows go into the manifest. Any change to this contract goes through the PM first.
```

Forge notes (a) and (b) add the class C size 1500 x 1500 and limit the review fields to Kimi
reviews in `reviews.kimi`.

## Red evidence

The test file is `tests/storytime-muse-delivery.test.ts`. It holds ten tests, T152 to T161.
Each test carries one rule of the plan task.

The tests use real 4000 x 3000 and 1500 x 1500 PNG files. One buffer of each shape is cached, so
the file stays fast. The tests read no path under `out/`, `/tmp`, or the Workbooks tree.

